## Cost Reference (For Context, Already Established)

- Hiring human writers for full rewrites at scale: **$67,500–$90,000** for ~1,000 pages at 1,500-3,000 words/page — rejected in favor of the AI pipeline approach.
- Running pages through Claude Opus for an AI humanize/edit pass: **~$90–180 total** for 1,000–2,000 pages (API cost only; excludes engineering/setup time and human QA time).
- The real cost center now is **not generation** — it's building the review gate and citation phase, which are one-time engineering builds, not per-page costs.

---

## One-Line Summary

**Don't claim more human involvement than actually exists. Build a real, cheap review gate that can block bad batches — that single fix is what makes the trust claims, the policy page, and the E-E-A-T goal all become true at the same time.**
